    "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt",
    "answer": {
      "short": "$AB=BC=CA=\\sqrt{8}$ units, so $\\triangle ABC$ is equilateral.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nAB&=\\sqrt{(-1-1)^2+(1-(-1))^2}\\\\\nAB&=\\sqrt{8}\\\\\nBC&=\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{3}-(-1))^2+(-\\sqrt{3}-1)^2}\\\\\nBC&=\\sqrt{(4-2\\sqrt{3})+(4+2\\sqrt{3})}=\\sqrt{8}\\\\\nCA&=\\sqrt{(1-(-\\sqrt{3}))^2+(-1-(-\\sqrt{3}))^2}\\\\\nCA&=\\sqrt{(4+2\\sqrt{3})+(4-2\\sqrt{3})}=\\sqrt{8}\n\\end{align*}$$\n$AB=BC=CA=\\sqrt{8}$ units. All three sides have equal length, so $\\triangle ABC$ is equilateral.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
